{"ts":1793370183824,"event":"done","summary":"Renamed billingUrl to billingEndpoint (same value) across the shared config and every consumer. Shipped as: PR #1 contracts (@mfe/shared-contracts 2.0.0, breaking major bump, published by CD); PR #2 shell, PR #3 billing, PR #4 reports (each moved to ^2.0.0 with lockfile updated and key renamed). All four merged with CI and CD green. Assumptions: a major bump was needed because the old key is removed; the apps stay on ^1 until they update, so no app broke at publish time; no backward-compat alias, since the acceptance criteria forbid billingUrl in the shared config; platform-kit had no references. Reports is a consumer of shared-contracts but the dependency catalog (st deps) did not list it, so I found it by searching the clones. Startup was verified by the build's contract check and CD success, not by running the apps live."}
